board and dashboard colour when stdout is a terminal and `NO_COLOR` is unset. kanban-md also takes `--no-color`. A root option `--no-color` next to `--dir` that disables colour for the one call is cheap and is what a user types when a pager mangles escapes. Both renderers carry the same test (`-t STDOUT && !$ENV{NO_COLOR}`) as a copy; move it into one place while adding the flag. Changes entry.

Pointers: Cmd::Board around line 203 and Cmd::Dashboard around line 249 each hold a copy of the colour test. The root option goes next to option done in lib/App/karr.pm and has to reach the command the way --dir does (see the argv handling there). Acceptance: output under --no-color is byte-identical to output under NO_COLOR=1.

